{"model": "glm-4.7-flash:q8_0", "created_at": "2026-10-21T20:01:09.183732418Z", "response": "**Problem 1**  \nMaria buys 7 notebooks at $4 each \u2192 $28, and 12 pens at $1.50 each \u2192 $18. Total = $46. 10% discount = $4.60. Amount paid = $46 - $4.60 = $41.40.\n\n**Problem 2**  \nLet Cara\u2019s age = \\(C\\). Ben\u2019s age = \\(B\\).  \n\\(B = 2(C - 6)\\). In 4 years, \\(B + 4 = 30\\) \u2192 \\(B = 26\\).  \nThen \\(26 = 2(C - 6)\\) \u2192 \\(C - 6 = 13\\) \u2192 \\(C = 19\\).\n\n**Problem 3**  \n- Ben drinks juice (clue c).  \n- Cleo does not drink tea (d) \u2192 Cleo drinks coffee (since juice is taken).  \n- Dog owner drinks coffee (b) \u2192 Cleo owns the dog.  \n- Alice does not own fish (a) \u2192 Alice owns cat (dog is taken).  \nThus Ben owns the fish.  \n\n**Problem 4**  \nDifferences: 4, 6, 8, 10 \u2192 next difference 12 \u2192 30 + 12 = 42.  \n(Or pattern: \\(1\\times2, 2\\times3, 3\\times4, 4\\times5, 5\\times6\\) \u2192 next \\(6\\times7 = 42\\).)\n\n**Problem 5**  \n\u201cAll but 9 die\u201d means all except 9 die, so 9 survive.\n\n**Problem 6**  \nPipe A rate = \\(1/6\\) tank per hour. Pipe B rate = \\(1/3\\) tank per hour. Combined rate = \\(1/6 + 1/3 = 1/2\\) tank per hour \u2192 time = \\(1 / (1/2) = 2\\) hours.\n\n**Problem 7**  \n1 kilogram = approximately 2.2 pounds, so a kilogram is heavier. A kilogram of feathers is heavier than a pound of steel.\n\n**Problem 8**  \nRetail price = \\(1.25\\) \u00d7 cost. 20% discount \u2192 sale price = \\(1.25 \\times 0.8 = 1.0\\) \u00d7 cost \u2192 100% of original cost.\n\n**Problem 9**  \nIf X were a liar, his statement \u201cAt least one of us is a liar\u201d would be false, meaning both are truth-tellers, contradicting X being a liar. Thus X is a truth-teller. Since the statement is true, at least one is a liar \u2192 Y is the liar.\n\n**Problem 10**  \n\\(3x + 7 = 2x + 15\\) \u2192 \\(x = 8\\).\n\n**Problem 11**  \nNumber of committees from 5 candidates choose 3: \\(\\binom{5}{3} = 10\\).\n\n**Problem 12**  \nDan > Ellie, Farah > Ellie, Farah < Dan \u2192 Dan > Farah > Ellie. Tallest: Dan, shortest: Ellie.\n\n---\n\nANSWER 1: 41.40\nANSWER 2: 19\nANSWER 3: Cleo owns the dog; Ben owns the fish.\nANSWER 4: 42\nANSWER 5: 9\nANSWER 6: 2\nANSWER 7: A kilogram of feathers\nANSWER 8: 100%\nANSWER 9: X is a truth-teller; Y is a liar.\nANSWER 10: 8\nANSWER 11: 10\nANSWER 12: Dan, Ellie", "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "context": [154822, 154824, 154827, 50, 3948, 678, 220, 98886, 5322, 3685, 13, 6928, 697, 975, 421, 498, 1366, 11, 714, 369, 93619, 3491, 11, 6248, 448, 198, 64, 1555, 304, 4063, 6823, 8929, 419, 3561, 320, 603, 817, 3491, 11, 304, 1973, 11, 518, 279, 1602, 835, 315, 697, 2033, 7731, 11686, 39139, 220, 16, 25, 366, 21680, 4226, 397, 11686, 39139, 220, 17, 25, 366, 21680, 4226, 397, 9335, 11686, 39139, 220, 98886, 25, 366, 21680, 4226, 1339, 1336, 21647, 1447, 16, 13, 362, 8060, 30656, 77903, 369, 400, 19, 1817, 323, 22542, 369, 400, 16, 13, 99200, 1817, 13, 22955, 49214, 220, 22, 77903, 323, 220, 98886, 22542, 11, 1221, 5221, 264, 220, 98668, 4, 11084, 389, 279, 2790, 13, 2585, 1753, 1558, 1340, 2291, 11, 304, 11187, 1939, 17, 13, 7355, 374, 10912, 438, 2310, 438, 78280, 572, 220, 21, 1635, 4134, 13, 758, 220, 19, 1635, 11, 7355, 686, 387, 220, 99064, 13, 2585, 2310, 374, 78280, 1431, 1939, 18, 13, 14503, 4780, 1959, 29296, 11, 7355, 11, 323, 35820, 78, 1959, 1817, 1828, 6896, 825, 6753, 320, 4616, 11, 5562, 11, 476, 7640, 8, 323, 1817, 10697, 825, 7027, 320, 80930, 11, 10794, 11, 476, 22754, 4292, 256, 2435, 1137, 25, 320, 64, 8, 29296, 1558, 537, 1828, 279, 7640, 13, 320, 65, 8, 576, 5562, 6372, 20940, 10794, 13, 320, 66, 8, 7355, 20940, 22754, 13, 320, 67, 8, 35820, 78, 1558, 537, 7027, 15231, 624, 256, 10474, 24187, 279, 5562, 11, 323, 1128, 6753, 1558, 7355, 1828, 1939, 19, 13, 3555, 374, 279, 1790, 1372, 304, 279, 8499, 25, 220, 17, 11, 220, 21, 11, 220, 98886, 11, 220, 98360, 11, 220, 99064, 11, 23688, 20, 13, 362, 36216, 702, 220, 99419, 